      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick checklist for wcag 2.1 compliance? mostly looking for stuff on color contrast ratios and making sure screen readers work right for a new fintech app we're building",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For WCAG 2.1 compliance in your fintech app, ensure all text has a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 against its background, increasing to 7:1 for large text, which is critical for financial information readability. Verify that color isn't the only way to convey critical meaning, so screen readers can still interpret data accurately without relying on visual cues. Additionally, map all interactive elements like buttons and links to clear functional names and roles so assistive technologies can announce them correctly to visitors. Finally, test your app with a screen reader module to ensure all forms, alerts, and financial data tables are navigable and provide appropriate error messages.",
