    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. can u expand a bit on the screen reader part? like what are some common things that get missed or cause issues during testing? we want to make sure we catch any weird bugs early.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common issues during screen reader testing often involve role confusion, like labeling image backgrounds as text content or mishandling alt attributes for illustrative diagrams in your fintech interfaces. Developers frequently forget that screen readers announce focus order, causing users to skip critical navigation elements like skip-to-content links or expected order links within data tables. Additionally, dynamic content updates, such as live transaction messages or loading spinners, are often missed because scripts do not properly announce updates or trap the user in an aria-live region. Always verify that custom components thoroughly implement all ARIA properties and do not break the standard hypertext semantics that browsers expect for accessibility compliance.",
      "source": "target",
